      "content": "It's certainly understandable to be concerned about medical expenses. Nonetheless, self-medicating without knowing specifics about your allergic reaction can be dangerous, especially with antihistamines.\n\nEveryone's allergic reactions and symptoms are different; what's safe in one scenario might not be safe in another. An incorrect dose or a non-recommended way to deal with your symptoms could lead to more harm.\n\nIt might help if you contact your local urgent care clinic to explain the situation. They can provide immediate advice, and many offer payment plans or sliding scale fees based on your situation. They may also be able to recognize some of your symptoms from experience even without being able to see you in person.\n\nPlease, don't delay in seeking advice. If you are having trouble breathing, swallowing, or experiencing significant discomfort, consider going to an urgent care facility or the emergency room. Your health and safety are worth that investment.",
